 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "In this town, every morning,",
   "start": 0.12,
   "end": 1.373
  },
  {
   "text": "everyone gets a letter from their future self.",
   "start": 1.423,
   "end": 3.511
  },
  {
   "text": "Buy gold today.",
   "start": 3.811,
   "end": 4.767
  },
  {
   "text": "Don't eat the fish on Tuesday.",
   "start": 4.947,
   "end": 6.319
  },
  {
   "text": "Do not marry Kevin.",
   "start": 6.499,
   "end": 7.502
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody here ever makes a mistake.",
   "start": 7.802,
   "end": 9.429
  },
  {
   "text": "Except Max.",
   "start": 9.729,
   "end": 10.474
  },
  {
   "text": "Max has never gotten a single letter.",
   "start": 10.774,
   "end": 12.545
  },
  {
   "text": "Every morning, his mailbox is empty.",
   "start": 12.665,
   "end": 14.532
  },
  {
   "text": "He buys the wrong stocks, he eats the bad fish, and everyone thinks he's cursed.",
   "start": 14.782,
   "end": 18.307
  },
  {
   "text": "Then one morning, his mailbox exploded.",
   "start": 18.707,
   "end": 20.627
  },
  {
   "text": "Hundreds of letters. All from future Max.",
   "start": 20.927,
   "end": 22.899
  },
  {
   "text": "And every single one said the same thing.",
   "start": 23.099,
   "end": 24.903
  },
  {
   "text": "Do not let the mayor do what he's about to do.",
   "start": 25.253,
   "end": 27.177
  },
  {
   "text": "So that night, Max sneaked into the mayor's mansion.",
   "start": 27.627,
   "end": 30.035
  },
  {
   "text": "He crawled past the guards, hid behind the curtains, and watched the mayor open his own letter.",
   "start": 30.235,
   "end": 34.538
  },
  {
   "text": "It said: burn the town to the ground.",
   "start": 34.938,
   "end": 36.533
  },
  {
   "text": "And the mayor always does what his letter says.",
   "start": 36.933,
   "end": 39.007
  },
  {
   "text": "Max ran to warn everyone.",
   "start": 39.357,
   "end": 40.713
  },
  {
   "text": "But who believes the cursed kid with no letters?",
   "start": 40.863,
   "end": 43.032
  },
  {
   "text": "The guards caught him, and locked him in the basement.",
   "start": 43.332,
   "end": 45.472
  },
  {
   "text": "No letter could tell him what to do now.",
   "start": 45.822,
   "end": 47.539
  },
  {
   "text": "So for the first time, someone in this town had to figure it out alone.",
   "start": 47.789,
   "end": 50.808
  },
  {
   "text": "He stacked the boxes, squeezed through the tiny window, and sprinted to the square.",
   "start": 51.108,
   "end": 54.676
  },
  {
   "text": "The mayor was striking the first match.",
   "start": 54.926,
   "end": 56.579
  },
  {
   "text": "Max dove.",
   "start": 56.879,
   "end": 57.605
  },
  {
   "text": "The match landed in a puddle.",
   "start": 57.955,
   "end": 59.252
  },
  {
   "text": "And the mayor's letter fell out of his pocket.",
   "start": 59.552,
   "end": 61.344
  },
  {
   "text": "The whole town read it.",
   "start": 61.544,
   "end": 62.644
  },
  {
   "text": "The mayor got the basement. Max got a parade.",
   "start": 62.994,
   "end": 65.231
  },
  {
   "text": "And the next morning, there was finally one letter in Max's mailbox.",
   "start": 65.631,
   "end": 68.871
  },
  {
   "text": "It said: told you.",
   "start": 69.271,
   "end": 70.236
  }
 ]
}